@param String intakeUrl
@param boolean production = false
<section class="calc-investigation" id="records-investigation" aria-labelledby="calc-investigation-title">
    <a class="calc-investigation-photo" href="${com.example.septic.web.StudioGuideRoutes.route("/septic-record-brief-example/roane/", production)}" aria-label="Read the Roane County investigation"><img src="/images/studio/oak-pasture-v1.webp" alt="Illustrative rural landscape, not the customer's property" width="1672" height="941" loading="lazy"><span>Illustrative landscape</span></a>
    <div class="calc-investigation-copy"><p class="studio-overline">Real case / Roane County, Tennessee</p><h2 id="calc-investigation-title">The listing stopped.<br>The research didn’t.</h2><p>The listing could not show the underground layout. A focused archive request recovered a historical permit and sketch. We explained what their markings could—and could not—establish.</p>
    <ol class="calc-research-steps">
        <li><span aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><h3>Follow the property clues</h3><p>We assembled the property identifiers. An empty public search was a limit, not proof that no file existed.</p></div></li>
        <li><span aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><h3>Request the missing record</h3><p>We requested the permit, layout, final approval and repair records through the TDEC archive route.</p></div></li>
        <li><span aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><h3>Explain the returned file</h3><p>The customer received the original agency file and a two-page explanation. Exact present-day location and condition remained unverified.</p></div></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="calc-case-actions"><a class="studio-button" href="${com.example.septic.web.StudioGuideRoutes.route("/septic-record-brief-example/roane/", production)}">Read the investigation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="${com.example.septic.web.StudioGuideRoutes.route("/septic-record-brief-example/", production)}">Explore all cases →</a></div>
    <p class="studio-fine">This case illustrates our approach, not record availability for your property.</p></div>
</section>
<section class="calc-records-cta" aria-labelledby="calc-records-title">
    <div><p class="studio-overline">Take the next step</p><h2 id="calc-records-title">What does your<br>property’s file say?</h2><p>We can look for the approved design, recorded layout and repair history—and explain gaps in the available file.</p><a class="studio-button" href="${intakeUrl}">Ask about my property <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="studio-fine">Your state and project details carry over. You can review and edit them before sending.</p><a class="calc-service-link" href="#quote-request" data-open-service>Looking for project service follow-up instead? ↗</a><p class="studio-fine">Records research—not a construction quote or site inspection. A record may not exist or establish current condition.</p></div>
    <img src="/images/studio/buyer-folio-v1.webp" alt="SepticPath research booklet, illustrative brand image rather than an agency record" width="1672" height="941" loading="lazy">
</section>
